---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import PageHero from "../components/PageHero.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../components/CodeBlock.astro";
import { snippets, commands, paths, support } from "../data/facts";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/?$/u, "/");
const mcp = paths.find((p) => p.id === "mcp")!;
---

<Base title="AI agents: give Claude a WhatsApp number over MCP | open-wa" description="open-wa's built-in MCP server exposes each Easy API method as a tool for Claude, Cursor and Windsurf. Config, start command and Claude Desktop setup.">
  <PageHero title="Give your agent a WhatsApp number" lede={mcp.what} />
  <section class="doc wrap doc-grid">
    <h2>1. Turn on the MCP server</h2>
    <p>Add an <code>mcp</code> block to your config:</p>
    <CodeBlock code={snippets.mcpConfig} lang="js" label="wa.config.mjs" />

    <h2>2. Start it</h2>
    <CodeBlock code={snippets.mcpStart} lang="bash" label="Terminal" />
    <p>Scan the QR code as usual. The MCP endpoint is then live at <code>{commands.mcpEndpoint}</code>.</p>

    <h2>3. Point your agent at it</h2>
    <p>For Claude Desktop:</p>
    <CodeBlock code={snippets.claudeDesktop} lang="json" label="claude_desktop_config.json" />
    <p>Cursor and Windsurf take the same URL and <code>X-API-Key</code> header in their MCP settings.</p>

    <h2>Which methods become tools</h2>
    <p>Each Easy API method is exposed as a tool. The licence rules follow the method: a method marked insiders or restricted needs that key on the number the agent is using, and every free method works without one.</p>
    <div class="note">
      <strong>Your agent, your account</strong>
      <p>An agent sending messages carries the same ban risk as any automation. Keep a person in the loop for anything that messages people who haven't written to you first. <a href={`${base}legal/#risk`}>Risk note</a>.</p>
    </div>
    <p><a class="btn btn-ink" href={`${base}quickstart/`}>Quick start</a> <a class="btn" href={support.docs}>MCP docs<span class="ext" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></p>
  </section>
</Base>
